---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Custom Text"
description: "Drop a .txt, .md, .epub, or .pdf file or paste a chapter. Whole books, read by chapter or by segment, saved on your device."
---
<header class="page__head">
  <h1>Custom text</h1>
  <p class="page__subtitle">Drop a <code>.txt</code>, <code>.md</code>, <code>.epub</code>, or <code>.pdf</code> file — or paste a chapter. Sanitized and saved on this device. Whole books are fine: nothing is trimmed.</p>
  <p class="page__subtitle">Every saved text can be read <strong>two ways, always both available</strong>: by <strong>segment</strong>, ~500 characters at a time, or by <strong>chapter</strong>, six paragraphs a page, the way the <a href="/library/">library</a> reads. Chapters come from the file's own headings — an EPUB's chapters, or <code>CHAPTER I</code>, <code>##</code> markdown headings and the like in a plain file. If there are no headings, the chapter view is simply the whole text, six paragraphs at a time.</p>
</header>

<div class="custom-form">
  <div class="uploader" id="uploader">
    <span class="uploader__title">Drop a .txt, .md, .epub, or .pdf file</span>
    <span class="uploader__hint">or click to browse — a whole book is fine, it gets split into segments</span>
    <input class="uploader__file" id="uploader-file" type="file" accept=".txt,.md,.epub,.pdf,text/plain,text/markdown,application/epub+zip,application/pdf">
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <label for="paste-title">Title</label>
    <input type="text" id="paste-title" placeholder="My chapter">
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <label for="paste-text">Or paste text</label>
    <textarea id="paste-text" placeholder="Paste any text here…"></textarea>
  </div>
  <div class="ocr-panel" id="ocr-panel" hidden>
    <p class="ocr-panel__lead" id="ocr-summary"></p>
    <ul class="ocr-panel__list" id="ocr-changes"></ul>
    <label class="ocr-panel__toggle">
      <input type="checkbox" id="ocr-clean" checked>
      <span>Clean up OCR noise</span>
    </label>
    <p class="ocr-panel__hint">Untick to keep the file exactly as it came — here, and every time you type it.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="custom-form__notice" id="chapter-notice" hidden></p>
  <p class="custom-form__notice" id="paste-notice" hidden></p>
  <div class="custom-form__row">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="paste-save">Save text</button>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Saved texts</h2>
<div id="saved-list" class="saved-list"></div>
